                        "sense_id": "79a815eb-3fd3-3b3e-a1d4-a1ee0d220546",
                        "entry_id": "75da47ee-80c1-35bb-a560-4502acace28b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a smiling manner; with a smile."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5bc1949-8bc9-484f-857f-664403e95199",
                                "sense_id": "79a815eb-3fd3-3b3e-a1d4-a1ee0d220546",
                                "text": "But me thinks at these words I heare some smilingly say, I would be loath to lacke liuing of my own till the Prince gaue me a maner of new Elme for my riming […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bfa9d836-310a-416d-8adc-c52d63b21f01",
                                "sense_id": "79a815eb-3fd3-3b3e-a1d4-a1ee0d220546",
                                "text": "But his flaw’d heart,\nAlack, too weak the conflict to support!\n’Twixt two extremes of passion, joy and grief,\nBurst smilingly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0742e85c-ab7a-4bc0-8c29-b641aef38d4e",
                                "sense_id": "79a815eb-3fd3-3b3e-a1d4-a1ee0d220546",
                                "text": "1753, Samuel Richardson, The History of Sir Charles Grandison in a Series of Letters, London: William Miller, 1811, Volume II, Letter 28, p. 279,\nHe looked smilingly serious."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7307858d-d47b-4299-b4ff-c81390cbc17d",
                                "sense_id": "79a815eb-3fd3-3b3e-a1d4-a1ee0d220546",
                                "text": "Lo! how they murmur, laugh, and smile, and weep:\nSome with upholden hand and mouth severe;\nSome with their faces muffled to the ear\nBetween their arms; some, clear in youthful bloom,\nGo glad and smilingly athwart the gloom;\nSome looking back, and some with upward gaze;\nYes, thousands in a thousand different ways\nFlit onward […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5074cccd-e807-4a13-b3e6-c1093ed15978",
                                "sense_id": "79a815eb-3fd3-3b3e-a1d4-a1ee0d220546",
                                "text": "So Amelia gave Dobbin her little hand as she got out of the carriage, and rebuked him smilingly for not having taken any notice of her all night."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "33916350-3415-41dc-b5de-03d26c87b9b1",
                                "sense_id": "79a815eb-3fd3-3b3e-a1d4-a1ee0d220546",
                                "text": "[…] Thorndyke, having unstrapped the hamper with as much care as if it contained a collection of priceless porcelain, bore it tenderly up to his bedroom; whence he appeared, after a considerable interval, smilingly apologetic for the delay."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7832a847-717d-4413-a837-8b83a403ca2d",
                                "sense_id": "79a815eb-3fd3-3b3e-a1d4-a1ee0d220546",
                                "text": "\"Don't tell me, Daddy, that you with all your complex brain and wonderful self are a thing with no more life hereafter than a broken clock!\" \"Four buckets of water and a bagful of salts,\" said Challenger as he smilingly detached his daughter's grip."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
